CORRECTION, added 2026-09-21: this commit's message describes only part of what
it contains.

The message describes the Iris tenant-label fix, which is real and is here:
web/src/shell/IrisWorkspace.tsx and its test, 33 lines across the two.

The other 1,433 lines are the Eva agent integration, which was authored
separately and was sitting uncommitted in the shared working tree at
~/projects/airbrx/omnigent when this commit was made. It was swept in
unintentionally. Nothing was wrong with the Eva code and nothing was wrong with
the Iris fix; they simply are not the same change and this message names only
one of them.

What arrived here without being named:

  omnigent/airbrx/eva/            the agent module: bundle, config, package,
                                  policy, routes
  omnigent/cli.py                 Eva's startup registration block
  omnigent/server/app.py          Eva's router mount
  scripts/eva/                    the coordinator binding script
  docs/eva/RUNBOOK.md             the rollout runbook
  tests/airbrx/test_eva_*.py      80 tests

Because pushes to omnigent-airbrx-server deploy production, this commit put Eva
on omnigent.airbrx.ai. That deploy succeeded (CD run 35679756840) and the site
stayed healthy. It was harmless because Eva registers only when a coordinator
has OMNIGENT_EVA_CONFIG set, and none does, so she is present but inert: not
registered, not in the agent drawer, catalog empty.

Two things a later reader should not conclude from this commit:

1. That Eva was reviewed before deployment. She was not. The full server suite
   had not completed against this tree when it shipped.
2. That the Iris change and the Eva change were tested together. They were not.

This note is an annotation. The commit is published, deployed and built on, so
it is not being rewritten.

The underlying cause is worth more than the correction: several Claude sessions
were working in ONE checkout at ~/projects/airbrx/omnigent rather than in
per-session git worktrees. A second session reported the same accident earlier
the same day, sweeping two files it did not own into a commit on another branch.
Separate worktrees make it structurally impossible.
